>>
endobj
298 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (The core engineering objectives governing this DBMS Project-Based Learning project are structured as follows:)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
299 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (Modern multi-plot farm operations encounter severe management and agronomic bottlenecks due to disparate, uncoordinated data tracking methods. Farmers, agricultural supervisors, and commercial farm syndicates routinely track their seasonal operations across disparate physical daybooks, fragmented spreadsheets, or informal memory. Consequently, critical dependencies between historical soil fertility assays, optimum varietal growth durations, seasonal weather calendars, and chemical input applications are routinely overlooked. Injudicious pesticide and fertilizer issues lead to severe chemical over-dosage, soil salinity degradation, and escalating operational expenses. Furthermore, without unified digital records, farm managers cannot accurately correlate cumulative labor investments and input expenditures with the final harvested tonnage across specific crop varieties. This inability to establish field-level and variety-level financial transparency results in persistent operational deficits, unaccounted stock shrinkage during post-harvest storage, and suboptimal commercial sales realization. A robust, transaction-aware Relational Database Management System is therefore essential to digitize, normalize, and safeguard farm records within a unified, constraint- driven platform.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
300 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (1. Design a unified conceptual Entity-Relationship \(ER\) model spanning 14 key entities that fully capture multi-farm plot structures, soil nutrient levels, crop calendars, inputs, labor, irrigation, harvest lots, and commercial sales.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (2. Construct a fully normalized relational schema decomposed to Third Normal Form \(3NF\) to eliminate data redundancy and insertion/deletion/update anomalies.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
302 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (3. Enforce rigorous domain-level and cross-table business invariants using declarative primary/foreign keys, CHECK constraints, and ACID-compliant SQLite triggers.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
303 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (4. Formulate optimized SQL queries incorporating inner/left joins, subqueries, group aggregations, and analytical views to yield actionable insights into crop profitability, input usage, and yield per acre.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
304 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 99 0 R
/E (5. Develop and Validate an interactive front-end application supporting complete CRUD operations, parameterized SQL queries, live error reporting, and rigorous verification test suites.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
